summary:
  The picture for a cast device is the first candidate that is known at
  all, and when the device cannot fetch that one it gets no picture.

history:
  main.qml chose between the episode's cover, the track's cover and the
  station's logo and only then asked whether the winner was an http(s)
  address. A local sidecar cover (file://) in front of a station that has
  a logo on the web sent the television nothing. The choice moved to
  CastLogic.picture, which passes a candidate the device cannot fetch
  over for the next. This mutant stops at the first one that is set.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CastLogic.js

find:
          if (typeof known[i] === "string" && /^https?:\/\/[^\s\/]/i.test(known[i])) return known[i];

replace:
          if (typeof known[i] === "string" && known[i] !== "") return /^https?:\/\/[^\s\/]/i.test(known[i]) ? known[i] : "";

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_castlogic.qml::test_the_picture_is_the_first_thing_known_that_a_device_can_fetch.
  Line-neutral.
